      "on_screen": [
        "One sentence with two ands",
        "= two projects disguised as one.",
        "The 'and' is a tell."
      ],
      "narration_text": "The one-sentence constraint is not about writing style. It is an elevator test for whether you know what you're building. A sentence with two ands is two systems dressed as one — different users, different inputs, different done-conditions. The refusal forces the decision that the list of features was deferring. Seth had thought he was building one thing. He was postponing a choice. The fourteen minutes is not wasted time. It is the essential work.",
      "estimated_duration": 22,
